&lt;p&gt;Thanks in advance!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150420073845im_/http:/typophile.com/files/pizzapalace_5873.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Need Help Identifying Laura Worthington Style Script Font</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/101228/</link><pubDate>Fri, 08 Mar 2013 09:57:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/101228/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Does anyone know what this script font is? I&amp;rsquo;ve identified lots of similar fonts, but none that are a match. Any help would be extremely appreciated! :) Thanks so much!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150418181949im_/http:/typophile.com/files/script%20font_6459.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>where can I buy/get this flourish???</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/69066/</link><pubDate>Fri, 02 Apr 2010 18:31:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/69066/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I know I have seen this before a few times so I know it must be out there somewhere&amp;hellip;can anyone tell me where I can buy it or even better if it is free : )&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131017091621im_/http:/typophile.com/files/Florish_4009.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>'Blazing' - A new limited edition print</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/68967/</link><pubDate>Wed, 31 Mar 2010 04:40:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/68967/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Hello all,&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m very pleased to say that I have produced a new art print.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The print is called &amp;lsquo;Blazing&amp;rsquo; and is available exclusively from Pictures on Walls.&lt;br&gt;
POW is a big gallery selling the work of some extremely talented and established artists including Banksy and Antony Micallef, so I think it&amp;rsquo;s a very positive development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;It&amp;rsquo;s an ambigram, which means you can read it both ways up. Details here:&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Calligraphy Workshops with Julian Waters at Cooper Union</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/68551/</link><pubDate>Fri, 19 Mar 2010 05:55:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/68551/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Two more workshops are being offered at Cooper Union this spring in lettering: &amp;ldquo;Organic Capitals&amp;rdquo; April 17 &amp;amp; 18 and &amp;ldquo;Compressed Styles (Black letter)&amp;rdquo; May 1 &amp;amp; 2. To see complete workshop details &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131012012207/http:/www.cooper.edu/ce" title="www.cooper.edu/ce"&gt;www.cooper.edu/ce&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;These workshops are appropriate for people who have some background in lettering or calligraphy and are already&lt;br&gt;
comfortable using a broad edged pen. Absolute beginners will struggle but if you&amp;rsquo;re up for the challenge Julian is an excellent teacher to begin with.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>(x) Endless - calligraphy style - Espresso {Mark S}</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/67312/</link><pubDate>Thu, 11 Feb 2010 08:30:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/67312/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Can someone please ID this typestyle. WTF would not work on it due to severe dithering&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131015095957im_/http:/typophile.com/files/endless_5563.gif" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>more details on rudolf koch please</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/67292/</link><pubDate>Wed, 10 Feb 2010 22:19:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/67292/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;hello.&lt;br&gt;
i would like to know more details about the typographer rudolph koch&amp;rsquo;s ties with the jewish community and his designs made for the jews, like the offenbacher haggadah.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;also, for hebrew readers, i wrote an essay about koch&amp;rsquo;s work in my hebrew blog:&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20130823072104/http:/cafe.themarker.com/view.php?t=1455233" title="http://cafe.themarker.com/view.php?t=1455233"&gt;http://cafe.themarker.com/view.php?t=1455233&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Beginner's calligraphy; and am I hampered by being a lefty?</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66795/</link><pubDate>Fri, 29 Jan 2010 05:40:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66795/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I know that there are already a few posts in the forum on beginning calligraphy, but I have slightly more specific needs. I&amp;rsquo;d like to learn calligraphy, especially since at some point I&amp;rsquo;d also like to do a bit of type design, and I have already come across a number of books on &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20141118184633/http:/www.amazon.com/s/ref=sr_st?keywords=calligraphy&amp;amp;rs=1000&amp;amp;page=1&amp;amp;rh=n%3A1000%2Ck%3Acalligraphy&amp;amp;sort=relevancerank"&gt;Amazon&lt;/a&gt; and elsewhere. The problem is that I&amp;rsquo;m not really sure if such books cater for left-handers, or if indeed it makes any difference at all. Any thoughts or specific recommendations?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Interesting Hebrew Manuscript</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66556/</link><pubDate>Sat, 23 Jan 2010 10:12:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66556/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414043420/http:/smg.photobucket.com/albums/v504/exfish/Jesuit%20manuscript/"&gt;found this&lt;/a&gt; at a relative&amp;rsquo;s house: a bound manuscript, text probably written in the 18th century, containing some Christian prayers in Hebrew and the text of Psalms. Looks to have been written by a Jesuit missionary, probably as an exercise in learning biblical Hebrew. As a specimen of calligraphy it&amp;rsquo;s pretty abysmal, but it gives interesting insight into an outsider&amp;rsquo;s perception of the Hebrew alphabet. The way the author (or possibly authors) structure the letters is often different from what I grew up with. Note especially the Mem, Shin, Tet and Pey. Some of the characters (the Mem especially) afforded me a minor epiphany or two about their typographic forms vs. handwritten. Also, the Aleph occasionally gets some pseudo-calligraphic swashiness.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Business Penmanship ::: released</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66498/</link><pubDate>Thu, 21 Jan 2010 13:56:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66498/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
SUDTIPOS ::: 01.2010 ::: NEW FONT RELEASE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Welcome back and happy new year. We are proud to announce the release of Business Penmanship and some amazing collateral material.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131015063925/http:/www.veer.com/products/typedetail.aspx?image=UMT0000507#specimen" title="http://www.veer.com/products/typedetail.aspx?image=UMT0000507#specimen"&gt;http://www.veer.com/products/typedetail.aspx?image=UMT0000507#specimen&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131015063925im_/http:/typophile.com/files/typophilebusiness_4941_4157.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
AN ILLUSTRATED PDF SPECIMEN&lt;br&gt;
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Specimen PDF is finally online. It is a beautiful collaboration with amazing illustrations by Leandro Castelao. Check it out!&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131015063925/http:/www.veer.com/download/pdf/businesspenmanship_specimen.pdf" title="http://www.veer.com/download/pdf/businesspenmanship_specimen.pdf"&gt;http://www.veer.com/download/pdf/businesspenmanship_specimen.pdf&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
SLIDESHOW SPECIMEN&lt;br&gt;
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Letters from Antarctica is a awesome slideshow by creative people from Veer.&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131015063925/http:/bit.ly/7vAHGY" title="http://bit.ly/7vAHGY"&gt;http://bit.ly/7vAHGY&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Learning Hebrew Calligraphy</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66157/</link><pubDate>Tue, 12 Jan 2010 11:41:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/66157/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;I&amp;rsquo;m interested in learning to do traditional &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414065346/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Hebrew"&gt;Hebrew&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150414065346/http:/typophile.com/wiki/calligraphy"&gt;calligraphy&lt;/a&gt;. Does anyone know where I might go for that in New York?&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Business Penmanship ::: Sudtipos 2010 release</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65968/</link><pubDate>Wed, 06 Jan 2010 06:34:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65968/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
SUDTIPOS ::: 01.2010 ::: NEW FONT RELEASE&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Welcome back and happy new year. We are proud to announce the release of &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131014232006/http:/www.veer.com/products/typedetail.aspx?image=UMT0000507#specimen"&gt;Business Penmanship&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; and some amazing collateral material.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131014232006im_/http:/typophile.com/files/typophilebusiness_4941.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
AN ILLUSTRATED PDF SPECIMEN&lt;br&gt;
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The long waited &lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131014232006/http:/www.veer.com/download/pdf/businesspenmanship_specimen.pdf"&gt;Specimen PDF&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is finally online. It is a beautiful collaboration with&lt;br&gt;
amazing illustrations by Leandro Castelao. Check it out!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;br&gt;
SLIDESHOW SPECIMEN&lt;br&gt;
/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131014232006/http:/bit.ly/7vAHGY"&gt;Letters from Antarctica&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; is a awesome slideshow by creative people from Veer.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Specimen slideshow release</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65941/</link><pubDate>Tue, 05 Jan 2010 09:45:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65941/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131013142144/http:/bit.ly/7vAHGY"&gt;Letters from Antarctica&lt;/a&gt; is a wonderful slideshow designed by the creative team of Veer to announce the launch of my new font &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20131013142144/http:/www.veer.com/products/typedetail.aspx?image=UMT0000507"&gt;Business Penmanship&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>MoMA | The Collection | Ryuichi Yamashiro. Forest. 1954</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65779/</link><pubDate>Wed, 30 Dec 2009 15:26:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/65779/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Prompted by Altaira&amp;rsquo;s new year&amp;rsquo;s kawai wish card ( &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317104647/http:/typophile.com/node/65762" title="http://typophile.com/node/65762"&gt;http://typophile.com/node/65762&lt;/a&gt;), and by Hrant&amp;rsquo;s quiz about the glyph used for the trees, I was reminded of one of my all time favourite calligraphy/typography posters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317104647im_/http:/typophile.com/files/tumblr_kuzyb2BWwg1qa8vs1o1_500_5138.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;br&gt;
&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150317104647/http:/www.moma.org/collection/browse_results.php?criteria=O%3AAD%3AE%3A6487&amp;amp;page_number=1&amp;amp;template_id=1&amp;amp;sort_order=1" title="http://www.moma.org/collection/browse_results.php?criteria=O%3AAD%3AE%3A6487&amp;amp;page_number=1&amp;amp;template_id=1&amp;amp;sort_order=1"&gt;http://www.moma.org/collection/browse_results.php?criteria=O%3AAD%3AE%3A&amp;hellip;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Scriptorium</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/49842/</link><pubDate>Thu, 25 Sep 2008 00:07:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/49842/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Scriptorium Fonts is an Austin, Texas based type foundry founded in 1992 by game designer, editor, writer and historian Dave Nalle. It specializes in adaptations of antique fonts and fonts based on artistic hand lettering drawn from the work of famous artists and calligraphers like Alphons Mucha, William Morris, Willy Pogany, Arthur Rackham and Howard Pyle.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Their catalog currently includes over 600 fonts and they have four type designers on staff: Dave Nalle, Michael Scarpitti, Peter Nevins and Kevin Andrew Murphy. Fonts include Abaddon, Hesperides, Buccaneer, Folkard, True Golden, Kelmscott, Ardenwood and Hendrix. They specialize in thematic packages of historic fonts based on specific artistic periods or design movements packaged together with licensed borders and art in the same style.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Turkey</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/38722/</link><pubDate>Thu, 01 Nov 2007 16:21:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/38722/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150419201259/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Indices"&gt;Indices&lt;/a&gt; : &lt;a href="http://web.archive.org/web/20150419201259/http:/typophile.com/wiki/Geography"&gt;Geography&lt;/a&gt; : Turkey&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
